	(text "Inputs: USB (J201) and dock (J303) ORed by Schottky diodes"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 17.78 38.1 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.8 1.8)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "f8943b88-9313-4cc6-a761-745aea9ea3fe")
	)
	(text_box "Values and why (datasheets: BQ24073 SLUS810N section 8.5; TPS63802 SLVSEU9D section 10; TPS22917 SLVSDW8B section 6)\n- Inputs: VBUS_USB and VBUS_DOCK each reach VIN_CHG through a PMEG2020EH Schottky (under 0.38 V at the input limit),\n  so neither input, nor a shorted dock pad, can back-feed the other or the USB host. TVS diodes sit at the connectors.\n  C101 4.7 uF (IN takes 1 to 10 uF) keeps the capacitance a USB host sees through D101 within USB's 10 uF.\n- ISET 2.0k: ICHG = KISET / RISET = 890 / 2000 = 0.445 A (KISET 797 to 975: 0.40 to 0.49 A), 0.45 C for the\n  1000 mAh pack. Precharge 88 / 2000 = 44 mA.\n- ILIM 3.3k: IIN = KILIM / RILIM = 1525 / 3300 = 0.46 A (KILIM 1330 to 1720 for 200 to 500 mA: 0.40 to 0.52 A),\n  USB 2.0 default power: the board has plain 5.1k Rd and does not read CC, and VIN-DPM is off in ILIM mode.\n  When the system load and ICHG together exceed the limit, the charger cuts ICHG (DPPM). Faster charging needs CC sensing.\n- EN2 100k to VIN_CHG, EN1 from GPIO45 with 100k to GND: (EN2, EN1) = (1, 0) selects the ILIM resistor on any input;\n  GPIO45 high gives (1, 1), USB suspend. The pull-up only draws current while input power is present\n  (EN pins have 285k internal pull-downs).\n- CE and TD to GND (charging enabled, termination on), TMR open (30 min precharge and 5 h fast-charge timers).\n- TS to the pack's 10k NTC on J101 pin 2: 75 uA bias, charging stops below about 0 to 4 C (VCOLD 2.1 V, 28k)\n  and above about 47 to 51 C (VHOT 0.30 V, 4.0k) for an NTC beta of 3950 to 3380.\n- TPS63802: VOUT = 0.5 x (1 + 560k / 100k) = 3.300 V; R2 = 100k is the datasheet maximum; MODE low (power save);\n  EN to VSYS (always on); L = 0.47 uH; 10 uF + 100 nF in, 2 x 22 uF + 100 nF out.\n  PG (open drain, 1 mA max) is TPS_PG: it pulls ESP_EN low through R212 1k (mcu_usb), so the module runs only in regulation.\n- TPS22917: CT 1 nF from CT to VIN, QOD tied to VOUT (fast discharge when the panel is switched off),\n  ON pulled down by 100k (GPIO46 strap must be low at reset).\n- MAX17048: CELL and VDD to VBAT, CTG and QSTRT to GND, ALRT only to TP107; I2C pull-ups are on the periph sheet."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20.32 223.52 0)
